kunzite (SM6475 parrot): the kernel-side topaz hardware defaults are unsafe here.
sweet_cpufreq_max() mapped khaje's 0xf523000 EPSS domain and faulted on the
first LUT read at boot #5 (Kernel data abort, pc _sweet_cpufreq_max+0x88,
far=VA+0x110 - the LUT offset), called from SweetBattery::start. Point it at
kunzite's two cpufreq-epss domains (0x17d91000 A55, 0x17d92000 A78, live
FDT) and make it READ-ONLY (print the LUTs; the PERF_STATE +0x920 write
offset is unverified on parrot - topaz's RCG lesson). SweetBattery defaults
to the static fallback (topaz I2C1/SPMI gauge MMIO not ported);
sweetbattery=1 re-enables the real poll for experiments.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@
